{
  "$comment": [
    "AUTHORED SEMANTICS for every procedural drawing in the library.",
    "",
    "`incompatibleTopics` is the field that matters most and the reason this file",
    "exists. Keyword matching gave a legal document for the word 'cave', and a",
    "document standing in for a cave is not a weak visual, it is a false one:",
    "with the audio off it tells the viewer something untrue. A hard reject on",
    "the wrong topic is what stops that, and it cannot be inferred from a name.",
    "",
    "`visualMeaning` says what the DRAWING communicates, not what the object is.",
    "A gavel means a ruling, not a hammer. The matcher scores against this.",
    "",
    "scripts/build-asset-library.js merges these with the drawing registry and",
    "writes config/assets/semantic-library.json. Anything registered but missing",
    "here is reported, never given defaults -- a silent default is how a generic",
    "filler ends up matching everything."
  ],
